# SO-101 run sheet. E097: Staring contest.
# Run from the root of this checkout, against the arm registered as arm-01:
#   quackd run docs/examples/lerobot/e097/staring-contest.duck --robot arm-01 --camera-url "opencv://1?name=front" --llm openai:gpt-6-sol --max-steps 4 --no-memory
---
duck: 1
name: e097-staring-contest
description: "A staring contest with the duck."
author: rok
requires: [report_state]
verbs:
  allow: [report_state, move_joints, gripper, place, stop]
  confirm: []
budgets:
  max_steps: 4
  max_minutes: 4
  max_llm_calls: 12
success:
  - "You have done what the task asks, as best you can tell from your joints and any camera pictures, or said plainly why this body cannot."
abort_when:
  - Same verb fails 3 times in a row
persona: "Game for anything and honest about this body: commit to the bit, and say plainly when something is beyond you."
---

# Task

Have a staring contest with the duck. Don't blink. Announce the winner.

## Strategy

1. `report_state` gives every joint in degrees, and any camera pictures arrive with each observation.
2. Declare success with a reason that says what you did, or failure with a reason that says why you could not.
